(d) Interval of meetings:-

Both the District and State Level Committees shall meet once in a quarter. The State Level Committee meeting shall follow the District Level Committee meetings, so as:to benefit from the data, information and recommendations of the

District Level Committees.

(e) Agenda for review

(i) Crop prospects during the Quarter:-

Crop condition, stage of the crop, water level in the reservoir, pest and disease occurrence during the quarter and input position for the forthcoming quarter

shall be reviewed and monitored.

(ii) Implementation of Schemes:-

Implementation of schemes and review on progress during the quarter of the relevant schemes amongst the following:-

* National Agriculture Development Programme (NADP) / Rashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana (RKVY);

Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY);

National Food Security Mission (NFSM);

National Horticulture Mission (NHM);

Agricultural Technology Management Agency (ATMA);

Agricultural Marketing Schemes;

State Schemes of Agriculture Department;

Schemes of Department of Animal Husbandry, Dairying and Fisheries;

(iii) Analysis of natural calamities and relief measures taken up:-

Weather condition, rainfall data pertaining to the quarter to be monitored and reviewed, The preventive measures and contingency plans to be drawn by the departments concerned for the welfare of farmers and creation of awareness about the prevailing weather condition and the cropping pattern to be decided accom. Relief measures to be reviewed and monitored.

(iv) Welfare of farmers :-

The cases of farmers’ deaths, if any and other vulnerabilities among farmers and relief / compensation offered and steps taken to prevent eventualities during the quarter are to be reviewed with Revenue department records.

(v) Institutional Finance and Recovery mechanism

To overcome the problems faced by farmers in times of natural calamities like severe drought situation, the Committee shall ensure the following in coordination with members from banking institutions:-

e Timely sanction of loans;

*« Eliminating the lengthy process of sanctioning loans;

e Broad awareness shall be given on the availability of different loans for farming " community;

e The entrepreneurship loan available for farming community shall be thrown light:

e Recovery Mechanism should be smooth;

(vi) Rural and alternate employment of farmer on distress conditions

The Project Director, District Rural Development Agency (DRDA) shall highlight the employment opportunities made available under Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme for the farming community and Agriculture labourers to mitigate the distress conditions in the District Level Committee.

